  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 220C, fan-forced. Line a large oven tray with baking paper. Peel the zucchini into ribbons with a vegetable peeler. Slice the tomato. Thinly slice the onion and haloumi.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2657464/photos/large/107460_1-83d7eb08244a8010bccf93ad4514a52a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pan-fry haloumi: Heat 1 tbs olive oil (see Make it faster) in a medium frypan over medium-high heat. Cook the haloumi, turning, for 2-3 mins until golden. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2657465/photos/large/107460_2-d59d452067cc9b91ba5a9ef25cc5397e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make sauce: Combine the tomato paste and half the red pesto in a bowl.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2657466/photos/large/107460_3-6ffb6411baf45dfb2f834d57327f36be.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake pizzas: Put 2 pita on the lined tray. Spread with the red pesto sauce and top with the tomato, onion, zucchini and haloumi. Scatter over the almonds and bake for 10-12 mins until golden.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2657467/photos/large/107460_4-19eb4abb78d636b7bcdb890bd49bdc50.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Combine the remaining red pesto, 1 tbs mayonnaise and 2 tsp water in a bowl. Cut the pizzas into wedges and drizzle with the red pesto mayo. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2657468/photos/large/107460_5-6677693db1d3c1c5bff0b4760f18d7f9.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it faster: Frying the haloumi before adding it to the pizzas gives golden and crispy edges, but if you're short on time just skip this step. It will still become warm and delicious while the pizzas are baking.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2657469/photos/large/107460_6-a126204f65a93fb97e50d4820773a47c.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
